{% comment %}
  Step 6 — post-booking success screen, shown after "Confirm payment" is
  tapped on the Confirmation step. No progress dots and no back button
  here on purpose (matches the Figma reference) — booking is done, there's
  nothing to go back to.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 438:7571), same instruction
  as the previous five steps: stay with the design, ignore backend
  integration.
  - Added the same shared kal-booking-flow-appointment-card.liquid used
    on Slot Picker/Patient Details, right below the intro — this screen
    didn't have one before.
  - "Reference No." row removed — not in the export. "Day & Time" renamed
    to "Date & Time" to match it.
  - "Payment" row is now dynamic (data-kal-confirm-payment), reflecting
    whichever card was selected on Confirmation's new Payment Method
    section ("Online payment" / "Pay at clinic") instead of the old
    always-"At the Clinic" text — see setPaymentMethod() in
    kal-booking-flow.js, which now also updates this alongside toggling
    the selected card.
  - "Before your visit" restyled from a bordered, inset card to a
    full-bleed tinted band (edge-to-edge, top/bottom border only, no
    corner radius) to match the export.

  CARD REDESIGN, later Figma pass (node 656:5433) — replaces the
  appointment-card + Consultation Details list above with one bordered
  "confirmed card" (.kal-confirmed-card) combining a date badge, the
  time/mode/relative-eta line, a dashed divider with the export's
  cutout-circle notches, a doctor row, and a Patient/Payment two-cell
  grid. Originally In-Clinic only (data-kal-mode-offline-only), with
  Video Consult keeping the older appointment-card + Consultation
  Details layout (no online-mode spec had been given for that pass) —
  per explicit instruction, this card is now shown for BOTH modes and
  that older layout is gone entirely. Mode/Patient reuse the exact same
  data-kal-confirm-mode/-name hooks renderConfirmationSummary() in
  kal-booking-flow.js already populates per mode, so no JS changes were
  needed; Payment stays the same static "₹450 Paid" mockup regardless of
  mode, same as this card already showed for In-Clinic.
  - "Booking ID AYR-20486" chip, new — added under the intro subtext, same
    generic addition regardless of mode.
  - Date badge (FRI/06/AUG), the "10:30 AM" time, and the "in 3 days"
    relative-eta chip are static mockup values straight from the export —
    same category as the doctor's photo/fee placeholders elsewhere in
    this flow, no hook exists (or is worth adding) to derive a day-badge
    + relative-day string from slotPicker's state for a screen this
    build isn't wiring to the backend anyway.
  - Mode/duration text reuses the existing data-kal-confirm-mode hook
    as-is (renderConfirmationSummary() in kal-booking-flow.js already
    populates it as "In Clinic - 30 mins") rather than introduce a
    second, differently-formatted mode hook just to match the export's
    exact "In-clinic, 30 mins" punctuation.
  - Patient cell reuses data-kal-confirm-name, same hook Confirmation's
    own details list already uses.
  - Payment cell is a static "₹450 Paid" per the export, NOT the old
    data-kal-confirm-payment text hook (which produced a plain "Online
    payment"/"Pay at clinic" string, not a price + paid badge) — now
    that the old per-mode appointment-card + Consultation Details layout
    is gone entirely, that hook has no matching element anywhere in this
    file; setPaymentMethod()'s querySelectorAll() over it no-ops
    harmlessly.
  - "Before your visit" band recolored from the mint tint to the export's
    sand/tan treatment (background, label, and icon-tint colors) and its
    check icons moved into their own white rounded-8 boxes; copy trimmed
    to the export's three items (arrival, ID + referral, reports) — the
    old "pay at reception" item is gone since payment is already settled
    per the new card above.
  - "Back to Homepage" button, new — a footer this step never had before,
    using the same shared .kal-step-doctor-select__continue treatment as
    every other step's primary CTA. Static mockup like the rest of this
    build — points at the shop's root URL, no click handler needed.

  Patient Name, Mode, and Date & Time reuse the EXACT SAME data-kal-confirm-*
  hooks as the Confirmation (review) step — renderConfirmationSummary() in
  kal-booking-flow.js already does flow.querySelectorAll() for each of
  those, so this step's matching elements get populated for free with zero
  JS changes.

  "Reschedule or cancel" (data-kal-reschedule-cancel) is now removed —
  explicit instruction, confirming it's genuinely absent from this
  screen's design rather than just scrolled out of the earlier export.
  It had no click handler wired up anyway (that's a separate,
  already-designed feature — localStorage token + minimal-info lookup —
  documented elsewhere, not part of this screen's build), so nothing else
  depended on it.

  The Confirmation step's "Confirm payment" button now also carries
  data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" (alongside its existing
  data-kal-confirm-booking hook) so the full flow is clickable through to
  this screen for demo purposes, even though nothing is actually booked
  yet on the backend.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — consolidated
  into the shared step shell (see "SHARED STEP SHELL" in
  kal-booking-flow.css), same correction as the Confirmation step: the
  success icon, intro, and full Consultation Details card were
  byte-for-byte identical between the old mobile and desktop blocks. The
  one real difference left is the "Before your visit" card, which the
  desktop Figma export omits entirely — hidden at 750px+ via CSS
  (.kal-step-booking-confirmed .kal-before-visit), the same technique
  used for Confirmation's pay-notice. No progress-dots/back-button on this
  step at any width (booking is done, nothing to navigate back to), so
  unlike the other consolidated steps there's no .kal-step-shell__header
  here — just a bare close button in the corner (.kal-step-booking-
  confirmed__header), same treatment as Therapy Confirmed's own __header:
  absolutely positioned rather than a normal-flow row, so it doesn't
  reserve height above .kal-step-shell__scroll and unbalance that region's
  justify-content:center (see kal-booking-flow.css's comment on that rule).
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed kal-step-shell">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info">
    <div class="kal-step-entry__info-content">
      <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading">You&rsquo;re all set</h2>
      <p class="kal-step-entry__body-text">Check the details before we hold it for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-step-entry__location">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--location">
        <!-- ICON: location-pin (not received yet) -->
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__location-text">
        Kerala Ayurveda Wellness Center, Indiranagar
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__header">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back" data-kal-close aria-label="Close">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'close' -%}
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
        Wraps the hero band + the card that sits partly on top of it
        (node 656:5433) in one plain block-flow group, deliberately NOT a
        flex column — .kal-step-shell__scroll's own flex gap would
        otherwise land between hero and card too and eat into the
        overlap below. The export's own structure nests these two the
        same way (no gap between them, unlike its wider 16/24px gaps
        elsewhere), so this wrapper is a container flattening fix, not a
        style choice of its own.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__summary">
        {%- comment -%}
          Mint hero band behind the success icon/heading — the export's
          own markup has this section overlap 24px behind the card below
          it (mb-[-24px] in the export), so the band's bottom edge tucks
          under the card's rounded top corners instead of stopping flush
          above it.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__hero">
          <div class="kal-confirmation-success-icon">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-success-icon__inner">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="kal-step-booking-confirmed__intro">
            <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Appointment confirmed</h2>
            <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">A confirmation is sent to your WhatsApp number.</p>
            <span class="kal-confirmed-booking-id">Booking ID AYR-20486</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          Now shown for BOTH modes (node 656:5433) — was In-Clinic only,
          with Video Consult keeping the older appointment-card +
          Consultation Details layout below (no online-mode spec had
          been given for that pass). Per explicit instruction, Video
          Consult now gets this exact same card too, so that older
          layout is removed. Mode/Patient reuse the exact same
          data-kal-confirm-mode/-name hooks renderConfirmationSummary()
          in kal-booking-flow.js already populates per mode ("Online -
          30 mins" vs "In Clinic - 30 mins") — zero JS changes needed.
          Payment stays the same static "₹450 Paid" mockup regardless of
          mode, same as this card already showed for In-Clinic.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="kal-confirmed-card">
          <div class="kal-confirmed-card__slot">
            <div class="kal-confirmed-card__date">
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__date-day">FRI</span>
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__date-num">06</span>
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__date-month">AUG</span>
            </div>
            <div class="kal-confirmed-card__slot-info">
              <p class="kal-confirmed-card__time">10:30 AM</p>
              <p class="kal-confirmed-card__mode" data-kal-confirm-mode>&mdash;</p>
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__eta">in 3 days</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmed-card__divider" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="kal-confirmed-card__divider-notch kal-confirmed-card__divider-notch--left"></span>
            <span class="kal-confirmed-card__divider-notch kal-confirmed-card__divider-notch--right"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmed-card__body">
            <div class="kal-confirmed-card__doctor">
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__doctor-avatar">NJ</span>
              <span class="kal-confirmed-card__doctor-info">
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__doctor-label">Your doctor</span>
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__doctor-name" data-kal-doctor-name-display>Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="kal-confirmed-card__grid">
              <div class="kal-confirmed-card__cell">
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__cell-label">Patient</span>
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__cell-value" data-kal-confirm-name>&mdash;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="kal-confirmed-card__cell">
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__cell-label">Payment</span>
                <span class="kal-confirmed-card__cell-value">
                  &#8377;450
                  <span class="kal-confirmed-card__paid-badge">Paid</span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Desktop-only omission handled in CSS, see this file's top comment.
        Also hidden for Video Consult (data-kal-mode-offline-only,
        toggled by applyConsultationModeVisibility() in
        kal-booking-flow.js) — "Pay at reception cash or card" and
        "arrive 10 minutes early" don't apply to an online visit.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-before-visit" data-kal-mode-offline-only>
        <p class="kal-before-visit__label">Before your visit</p>
        <ul class="kal-before-visit__list">
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Arrive 10 minutes early for check-in.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Bring an ID and your referral letter if you have one.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="kal-before-visit__item">
            <span class="kal-before-visit__icon">{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'check' -%}</span>
            <span>Carry any recent reports or prescriptions.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer">
      <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue">Back to Homepage</a>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>
